The following is an example of suspending at 90% of 1000 credits and immediately suspending at 100%. SUSPEND stops the warehouse after the currently executing statement completes, which may allow additional credits to be consumed beyond the quota, while SUSPEND_IMMEDIATE cancels the currently executing statement and immediately stops execution.

```sql
USE ROLE ACCOUNTADMIN;

CREATE OR REPLACE RESOURCE MONITOR limit1 WITH CREDIT_QUOTA=1000
  TRIGGERS ON 90 PERCENT DO SUSPEND
           ON 100 PERCENT DO SUSPEND_IMMEDIATE;

ALTER WAREHOUSE wh1 SET RESOURCE_MONITOR = limit1;
```

A warehouse can be allocated to only one resource monitor at the account level.
